sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-13> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Progressive change of growth ratios along a series of allied forms (orthogenesis) is real in some lineages, and the mathematical study of form can detect such series where they are not obvious, while also showing that strong resemblances of form may arise independently as numerical coincidences.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mathematical morphology can reveal orthogenetic series and warn of convergence";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XI, “The Logarithmic Spiral”; topic “Spiral form and phylogeny”. Scope: fossil and living lineages, especially molluscan shells"
}
